pack.go`: `Limits`, `DefaultLimits`, `Stats`, `Unpack`. Checks path, depth, length, `.git`, duplicates, case-fold collisions, paths under or over symlinks (either order), entry types and modes. Compressed, decompressed and ratio caps via counting readers. Symlinks are created last.\n- `internal/tarball/{unpack,pack}_test.go`: reject table, gzip bomb (streamed), modes, dest checks, bad input, round trip, Files root, skips, symlink-to-secret, root names, `FuzzUnpack`.\n- `docs/layout.md`: one line for the package.\n\n## Testing\n`go vet ./internal/tarball`, `go test ./internal/tarball` pass; `FuzzUnpack` ran 20s with no failures; seed corpus runs under plain `go test`.\n\n## Open issues\n- A NUL in an entry name cannot reach the unpacker through `archive/tar` (it cuts ustar names at NUL and the writer ignores PAX path records), so that check is covered by a direct `cleanName` unit test rather than an archive case.\n- Ratio cap of 100 can reject very compressible but legitimate output; the limit is in `DefaultLimits`.\n- Full `make test` was not run; only the new package and docscheck.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36506a4a-6b90-47de-9f0c-0eaf8d58cc0a","uuid":"e62f5e9d-aaf5-428c-b3a6-1b205c785964","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:14:18.333Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"4ef142f Merge branch 'main' into worker/engineer-314-kubernetes-executor-part-3-safe-tarball\n1433e2b ard(triage:lead): #346 This adds the first version of the `ard setup` command: a new setup pac… [skip ci]\n3685e91 ard(triage:lead): #344 This replaces the conflict and force handling in the init planner with… [skip ci]\nok  \tgithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball\t0.460s\tcoverage: 83.8% of statements\ngithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball/errors.go:14:\tnewError\t66.7%\ngithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball/errors.go:21:\tError\t\t0.0%\ngithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball/pack.go:57:\tPack\t\t76.5%\ngithub.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/tarball/pac